# Testing Standards

## Pyramid

| Layer | Command | When |
|-------|---------|------|
| Unit | `npm test` | Every change |
| Platform | `npm run test:platform` | Python/RAG/platform changes |
| Kind E2E | `./scripts/test-e2e-kind.sh` | Agent API, auth, chat, orchestration |
| Workflows | `./scripts/test-e2e-workflows.sh` | End-to-end run lifecycles |
| Full | `./scripts/test-all.sh` | Pre-merge / pre-deploy |

## Writing tests (Vitest)

- Place tests beside code: `shared/test/*.test.ts`, `agents/<agent>/test/*.test.ts`.
- Test real behavior (parsers, auth, dedupe, correlation) — not trivial getters.
- Use existing patterns in `shared/test/internal-auth.test.ts`, `shared/test/alert-correlation.test.ts`.
- E2E scripts use `e2e_curl` from `scripts/test-e2e-lib.sh` (loads `SRE_INTERNAL_TOKEN` from cluster secret).

## E2E auth

Kind E2E hits agents with `SRE_AUTH_STRICT=true`. Tests must send Bearer token via `e2e_curl`, not bare `curl -sf`.

Gitops endpoints may return HTTP 500 with `{ success: false }` — use `e2e_curl -s` (no `-f`) when asserting response body.

## Platform (pytest)

```bash
cd sre-agent-platform && python3 -m pytest tests/ -q
```

Add tests under `sre-agent-platform/tests/` for RAG, dedup, routing logic.

## CI vs local

- **CI** (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): unit + platform on every push/PR.
- **Local Kind E2E**: required for agent/helm changes before claiming "deployed and verified."
